<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Applying the general multiplication rule without replacement to committee selection</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A school debate club in Kisumu consists of <b>{@num_B@} boys</b> and <b>{@num_G@} girls</b>. The patron selects two learners at random, one after the other, to represent the school at a regional contest. Because a learner cannot be selected twice, this is a selection <b>without replacement</b>.</p>

<p>Let \(G_1\) be the event "the first learner selected is a girl" and \(G_2\) be the event "the second learner selected is a girl".</p>

<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that the first learner selected is a girl, \(P(G_1)\).</p>
<p><i>(Enter your answer as a fully simplified fraction).</i></p>
<p>\(P(G_1) =\) [[input:ans1]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>

<p><b>b) </b> Given that the first learner selected was a girl, find the probability that the second learner selected is also a girl, \(P(G_2 \mid G_1)\).</p>
<p>\(P(G_2 \mid G_1) =\) [[input:ans2]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>

<p><b>c) </b> Use the general multiplication rule to find the probability that <b>both</b> selected learners are girls.</p>
<p>\(P(G_1 \text{ and } G_2) =\) [[input:ans3]]</p>
<div>[[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>First, find the initial total number of learners in the club:<br>
\(\text{Total}_1 = {@num_B@} + {@num_G@} = {@total1@}\)</p>

<p><b>Part a: First Event</b><br>
The probability of selecting a girl on the first draw is the number of girls divided by the total number of learners:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(G_1) = \frac{{@num_G@}}{{@total1@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(G_1) = {@ta1@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part b: Conditional Probability</b><br>
Because the first learner is not replaced, there is now 1 fewer girl in the club, and 1 fewer total learner:<br>
New number of girls = \({@num_G@} - 1 = {@num_G_minus_1@}\)<br>
New total learners = \({@total1@} - 1 = {@total2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(G_2 \mid G_1) = \frac{{@num_G_minus_1@}}{{@total2@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(G_2 \mid G_1) = {@ta2@} } \)</p>

<p><b>Part c: General Multiplication Rule</b><br>
The general multiplication rule states that \(P(A \cap B) = P(A) \times P(B \mid A)\).</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(G_1 \text{ and } G_2) = P(G_1) \times P(G_2 \mid G_1) \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\( \displaystyle P(G_1 \text{ and } G_2) = \frac{{@num_G@}}{{@total1@}} \times \frac{{@num_G_minus_1@}}{{@total2@}} \)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\( \displaystyle \boxed{ P(G_1 \text{ and } G_2) = {@ta3@} } \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
